Definition

Exception Handling is the process of identifying, managing, and recovering from exceptions that occur during program execution.

Need for Exception Handling
1. Responsive Process

Handles errors that occur during run-time.

2. Precautionary Method

Prevents deviation from expected output.

3. Resume Execution

Allows the process to continue or restart from the interruption point.
----------------
TYPES:

(i)System Exception
Definition

A System Exception occurs when the automation process fails because of technical or system-related problems.

Causes
Network failure
Application crash
Database failure
Missing file
Server unavailable
Outlook failure

Example

Robot tries to open:

Plain Text
Invoice.xlsx

But the file is unavailable.

➡️ System Exception

Example from Slide

Outlook is not working.

Robot cannot open email attachments.

➡️ System Exception

Solution
Use Try-Catch activities
Retry Scope
Validation checks
Error-proof coding
-----------------------
5. Business Rule Exception
Definition

A Business Rule Exception occurs when a business rule
or condition is violated even though the system is functioning correctly.

Causes
Invalid data
Missing mandatory fields
Incorrect values
Business rule violations
Example

Business Rule:


Customer age must be above 18.
 

Input:


Age = 15

System is working.

Business condition fails.

➡️ Business Rule Exception

Example from Slide

The robot identifies emails based on a specific subject.

Expected:


Invoice Request

Actual:


Invoice
Invoice Req
Request for Invoice

Robot cannot identify the mail.

➡️ Business Rule Exception

Solution
Use standard formats
Data validation
Unique identifiers
Business rule checks
